@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+# Recorded offer comparison — build 2244
+
+Baseline inspection confirmed v1.22.28/build2243, commit 6ed905ce18832be10f04e47cac8a703af4895719, tree 9a6fb02bd00b789f6566cfb59f70868972b3ed2d. The actual existing comparison service reevaluates two to four proposals. An enforced-2-GiB disposable baseline replay observed two real evaluation calls, and the workspace renderer had no select-two assessed-offer journey. That legacy API remains unchanged.
+
+The new contextual action reuses completed assessment contexts and existing scoped tab storage. The existing Trade workspace holds at most two compact offers; it does not create another page, database, background operation or comparison API. Add, explicit replacement, removal and return leave the underlying draft and recommendation intact. Original asset order and exact player/pick IDs are separate from the existing order-insensitive evaluation identity. Pick labels retain verified original-franchise metadata. Opening and expanding the comparison perform no HTTP work.
+
+Shared lineup numbers require matching authorized workspace, league/franchise, ownership generation, canonical prepared-roster generation, scoring profile, projection source, season, week and projection generation. The prepared-roster identity is exposed from the profile the workspace already reads; it is not calculated again. Source conflicts, missing metadata, explicit staleness and unsupported/provisional full lineups withhold a joint numerical comparison. A supported independent effect remains visible when the other offer has incomplete lineup evidence under the same established identity. Missing is never zero. The no-trade baseline means no exchanged assets and, only with admitted numerical evidence, zero trade-related change.
+
+Captured decisions, counterparty cases, supported reserve disclosures and configured roster-space consequences remain attached to each offer. The comparison does not choose a winner, endorse an exploratory offer, change a recommendation or infer manager acceptance. Neutral Market evidence and Custom personal values retain their original separate fields. Different valuation modes/methods are explicitly labeled. Submitted Sleeper lineups remain separate from the analytical optimized lineups.
+
+Reloaded records are labeled RETAINED / NOT REVALIDATED. If their immutable identities still match the prepared workspace, recorded snapshot-relative effects can be inspected; the UI makes no new freshness or current-endorsement claim. Changed/aged publications, changed ownership, missing compatible preparation and known stale contexts withhold the shared comparison. Normal admission and evaluation remain necessary for a new assessment. Scope checks use the server-authorized workspace; a hash is not a new authorization mechanism.
+
+Selection takes an independent immutable copy of the completed context. Editing the live draft's valuation mode cannot mutate a selected assessment. A real canonical-source invalidation marks the stored assessments stale; Custom evidence additionally requires the known saved revision, selected method and personal publication identities to match the current prepared workspace. The reload controls separately prove complete retained comparisons and retention of a native incomplete Custom evaluation, without promoting incomplete evidence to supported.
+
+## Acceptance and preservation
+
+Focused controls use real authenticated routes, canonical evaluation and retained native fixture scores: a legal one-QB/FLEX/K/DEF roster, Superflex, a higher-gain/higher-cost pair, incomplete depth, an impossible post-trade starting lineup, source-generation changes, aging, Neutral/Custom differences, replacement/removal, exact ordering, reload and league switching. Four viewports are 320×432, 375×667, 390×844 and 1280×900, with keyboard and Chromium touch emulation. Physical iPhone/Safari and authenticated owner acceptance are not established by these fixtures.
+
+Initial failures are retained separately. They exposed missing static-script registration and assumptions in test setup: the packaged Node binary was not on PATH, an edited draft's board was still collapsed, Playwright cleanup was ordered incorrectly, a reused fixture lacked legal bench capacity, and a selector reached a hidden package variant. The fixture now uses actual legal configured capacity; no roster/admission assertion or qualification rule was weakened. Keyboard focus is tested after real keyboard input rather than mouse modality. The comparison action is visible before nested variants.
+
+No optimizer, scoring, fantasy source, Market/Custom formula, final bilateral qualification, source acquisition, FOIS grade, roster-capacity policy, saved preference, submitted lineup or resource reserve changes. The container cap remains 2 GiB, Trade 256+128 MiB and FOIS 768 MiB. Opening ordinary pages adds no discovery or provider work. Full exact-source mandatory validation and guarded Actions preparation/publication are required before release; the final external evidence package records completed outcomes and all original failed/incomplete attempts.
